    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d975">

                <pb facs="1474" n="1448" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/7–1954: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States
                            Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-19T13:00:00+01:00">July 19, 1954—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 660. Limit distribution. Dennis Allen has just informed us that London
                    has cleared Eden‘s messages to Colombo
                    powers, Australia and New Zealand (Sectos
                        644<anchor n="1" xml:id="d975-f1"/> and 649<anchor n="2" xml:id="d975-f2"/>)
                    including suggestion for statements along lines of proposed United States
                    unilateral declaration in event of Geneva settlement and instructed that
                    messages be delivered immediately.</p>
                <p>We will be discussing with British today program of action to be taken in event
                    agreement reached at conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
